Archive layer date: 2024-03-18; retrieved 2026-11-02.

Modified: the 8,006 Byer polygons (not summer-house areas) were transformed
from ETRS89 / UTM zone 32N (EPSG:25832) to WGS84 (EPSG:4326), rounded to
1e-7 degrees, delta-encoded and gzip-compressed. Rings and holes are retained;
no cartographic simplification, expansion or nearest-place assignment is applied.
Regenerate with data/prepare-dk-localities.py (Python 3.9+, DuckDB with spatial).

These are named built-up settlement areas, not postal districts, municipal
boundaries or a current national address register. Their 2024 extent can be stale
at later development boundaries. Index crosswalks omit ambiguous or unmatched
names; runtime recovery additionally requires source postal corroboration.
